gakj(){return"Measure immediately after waking, before getting up and before any activity such as speaking, sitting or drinking. Always at about the same time each morning and after sufficient sleep. Interruptions such as going to bed late, frequent night awakenings, alcohol or illness are marked as measurement disturbances. The measurement takes 5 minutes (vaginal or rectal) or 8 minutes (oral). Temperature is entered in steps of 0.05 K \u2014 that is precise enough, because thermometers, even digital ones showing two decimal places, typically measure to an accuracy of only 0.1 \xb0C to 0.05 \xb0C: values from 36.68 to 36.72 become 36.70, and values from 36.73 to 36.77 become 36.75."},
